    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If your roof insurance claim is denied, you should immediately review the denial letter and your policy to understand the exact reason for the rejection before taking steps to appeal.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "immediately review the denial letter and your policy to understand the exact reason for the rejection before taking steps to appeal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Review and Protect"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Protect the roof: Cover any leaks with a tarp right away, but avoid starting major repairs that could erase evidence."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Read the denial letter: Find the exact policy clauses and specific reasons your insurer rejected the claim."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Request your claim file: Ask your insurance company for all notes, photos, and reports from the original adjuster."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Gather Evidence"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get an independent inspection: Hire a trusted local roofing contractor or a HAAG-certified forensic inspector to document missed damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Collect local weather data: Pull official storm, wind, or hail reports for the exact date of the weather event."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Take detailed photos: Shoot wide angles and close-ups of the roof, vents, and gutters, using a coin or ruler for scale."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "File an Appeal"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Request a re-inspection: Ask for a second review with a different field adjuster, and have your independent contractor present on-site."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Submit a formal appeal: Send a clear written letter via certified mail addressing the denial points with your new evidence attached."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Escalate the Dispute"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Hire a public adjuster: Bring in an independent adjuster who represents you instead of the insurance company."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Contact state regulators: File a complaint with your state\u2019s department of insurance if you suspect unfair claim handling."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Consult an attorney: Speak with a property insurance lawyer if the denial involves bad faith or a very high repair cost."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "More advice can be found at United Policyholders .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "United Policyholders",
            "link": "https://uphelp.org/ask-an-expert/question/looking-for-advice-claim-denial-for-roof-damage-from-hail/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Why did the insurance company say they denied the claim (e.g., wear and tear, age, storm date)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What state are you located in?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more targeted next steps for your situation."
      },
